      "text": "To solve the given equation \\( x \\cdot (x + y) = x^2 + 8 \\), we will follow a step-by-step approach:\n\n1. **Expand the left-hand side of the equation:**\n   \\[\n   x \\cdot (x + y) = x^2 + xy\n   \\]\n\n2. **Set the expanded form equal to the right-hand side:**\n   \\[\n   x^2 + xy = x^2 + 8\n   \\]\n\n3. **Subtract \\( x^2 \\) from both sides to simplify:**\n   \\[\n   x^2 + xy - x^2 = x^2 + 8 - x^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   xy = 8\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{8}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( xy \\) is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
